      "disposition": "ADDED_MUTEX_INIT_ACCESS_MUTEX_AFTER_FLASH_SETUP",
      "details": "The reconstructed C mirror previously zero-initialized the access context but omitted the explicit __mutex_init present in stock Ghidra and assembly. The setup helper does not initialize this field. Added mutex_init(access.mutex) after the setup block and before the length branch, matching stock placement on both the successful setup path and the already-in-bootloader path. The exact .S remains selected by Kbuild and already contained the stock initialization, so this corrects the readable C mirror; it does not change the shipped candidate module. No active lock use of this local field in the read helper was established, so this is recorded as a source-parity defect rather than a proven stock runtime deadlock.",
