    {
      "id": "flash-output-buffer-lifetime",
      "category": "lifetime",
      "severity": "CALLER_BUFFER_RETAINED_BY_DESIGN_WITH_DEVICE_MANAGED_LIFETIME",
      "disposition": "NO_LOCAL_LEAK_PROVEN_OUTPUT_POINTER_STORED_IN_CALLER_BUFFER",
      "details": "devm_kmalloc allocates the requested flash output and stores it in buffer->data with buffer->buf_size. The function fills buffer->data_length and returns the buffer to its caller; it does not treat this as a temporary local payload. Resizing frees the old buffer when a managed device is available, and devres releases allocations on device teardown. The broader teardown of every external caller was not re-audited in this round.",
      "evidence": {
        "candidate_source_lines": "syna_tcm_read_flash_address.c:48-100",
        "stock_ghidra_decomp_lines": "0294_00124208_syna_tcm_read_flash_address.c:83-135",
        "stock_assembly": "0294_syna_tcm_read_flash_address_00124208.asm:0x1da98 devm_kmalloc; output pointer stored through caller buffer"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "conditional-old-output-buffer-retention-on-device-lookup-retry",
      "category": "lifetime",
      "severity": "CONDITIONAL_STOCK_DEVRES_RETENTION",
      "disposition": "INHERITED_STOCK_BRANCH_PRESERVED_INTERLEAVING_UNPROVEN",
      "details": "When an undersized output buffer already has data, the function tries to obtain a managed device before devm_kfree. If that lookup fails, it logs and retries. If a later lookup succeeds, the old pointer can be overwritten by the new allocation without an explicit free, retaining the old devres allocation until device teardown. Ghidra and stock assembly contain the same retry path. This lookup interleaving was not dynamically demonstrated; the exact stock assembly is preserved.",
      "evidence": {
        "candidate_source_lines": "syna_tcm_read_flash_address.c:49-86",
        "stock_ghidra_lines": "0294_00124208_syna_tcm_read_flash_address.c:86-118",
        "stock_assembly_calls": "0x1da6c syna_request_managed_device; 0x1da78 devm_kfree; 0x1da7c retry; 0x1da98 devm_kmalloc",
        "stock_assembly_sha256": "dbfd6f00363a8b92a0488003026a6cf2da7d5b81186e9c7747ac7b4fdedf4756"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "flash-access-context-cleanup",
      "category": "lifetime",
      "severity": "CONDITIONAL_DEVRES_RELEASE",
